    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i've been trying this box breathing thing (inhale 4, hold 4, exhale 4, hold 4) lately to help with stress. can u explain what's actually happening in the body when i do that? like how does it affect the nervous system or stuff like cortisol?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Box breathing activates your parasympathetic nervous system, which directly counters the \"fight or flight\" response to reduce stress. This physiological shift triggers the vagus nerve to signal your heart and lungs to slow down, effectively calming your immediate reaction to stress. Consequently, both the expression of cortisol (stress hormone) and physical symptoms like rapid heart rate decrease as your body moves from a state of high alert to one of calm. Over time, this practice helps retrain your nervous system to return to a relaxed state much faster when faced with anxious situations.",
      "source": "target",
